= Past Tense Verbs

Name: #box(width: 12em, stroke: (bottom: 0.5pt), height: 0.9em) #h(1fr) Date: #box(width: 7em, stroke: (bottom: 0.5pt), height: 0.9em)

A *past tense verb* tells about something that already happened. Many verbs add _-ed_ (jump → jumped). Some verbs change in special ways (go → went).

== Part 1: Fill in the Blanks

Write the past tense of the verb in parentheses to complete each sentence.

+ Yesterday, I #blank (walk) to school.
+ She #blank (eat) pizza for lunch.
+ The dog #blank (jump) over the fence.
+ We #blank (go) to the park on Saturday.
+ Tom #blank (see) a rainbow after the rain.
+ They #blank (play) soccer last night.
+ My mom #blank (bake) a cake for my birthday.
+ The bird #blank (fly) away from the tree.

